":{"commit_sha":"1db5b8d7a7c6d818184133c92141b319a066cdbe","position":"1788365507338467001-fbe351bd-1448-488e-aa89-a1a592eb86d6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2f9bc654d699ff9ac6efeab4ddc437c095a94ce9ca8d6b6cc5faf23d1c560c1e","event_uuid":"50fa9311-427d-4851-a082-2129a32c4db9","position":{"commit_sha":"4a3da06e243bb5df09f168b0898ac09b9abe0b58","position":"1788370493441603001-50fa9311-427d-4851-a082-2129a32c4db9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0f5cdff32ba29f6781046a773b6e10996a6752002b65dd5d5a65215f2604d18f","event_uuid":"0e0749cc-fa03-42ec-8766-d421e7e6daac","position":{"commit_sha":"5cfc100ba15b5b040f1c38a6bad8333e9813c797","position":"1788370955734079001-0e0749cc-fa03-42ec-8766-d421e7e6daac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA before repair (rebar-debug Phase 1):\n\nStep 0(a): searched for `gate_status REVIEW_RESULT sidecar stale findings terminal`, `gate_status`, and `REVIEW_RESULT gate_status`; current ticket is the active report. Prior related closed bug `d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231` introduced the async gate handle/poll surface, but did not cover REVIEW_RESULT readability.\nStep 0(b): ticket has no quoted version; created_at 1788332684139080595 maps to floor commit a85cb4781845ccf0d8c0375adce9a01391ba4bc8. No later changes to the suspect paths before current HEAD 384ca0dc2d7c.\nStep 0(c): fresh worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/debug-gate-status-sidecar` is at 384ca0dc2d7c (= origin/main).\n\nDesign-decision check: docs/plan-review-gate.md and AGENTS.md document `review_plan_start` -> poll `gate_status(job_id)` as the long-gate workflow, with terminal `passed/failed` carrying durable attestation currency. `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` documents `sidecar_emitted`, and the ticket explicitly allows either deferring terminal visibility or adding a readability indicator. No ADR/ticket found that intentionally permits terminal-with-stale-findings; this is a defect fix honoring the documented poll contract, not a contract change.\n\nProven mechanism: `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py:141-178` builds a terminal poll response solely from the `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` index record plus signed-attestation currency. It never checks whether the plan-review `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar for that run exists/readable. `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:148-179` records `status=passed`/`verdict=<BLOCK|PASS>` in the run index from the returned result, and `_terminal_from_result` treats a BLOCK verdict as `passed` (completed). For BLOCK there is no signed plan-review attestation, so the existing `durable` block is `unsigned` by design and cannot distinguish “findings not readable yet” from “BLOCK has no attestation.”\n\nRuntime proof: in a local scratch repo, I wrote an older `REVIEW_RESULT`, then recorded a terminal plan_review gate-run index for a newer job without writing a new sidecar. `gate_runs.gate_run_status(job_id)` returned `{'status':'passed','verdict':'BLOCK',...}` while `sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket)` returned the old finding (`old-finding`). This exactly reproduces the silent stale-read window.\n\nDefect origin: introduced by commit 44ec1c2e67373a2e2b888a1beb0bf1cb7b0f6d39 (`d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231: async gate start (P2)`), which added `gate_run_status` and documented terminal `passed/failed` without a per-run sidecar-readability token. Blame/log -L on `gate_run_status` points to that new-file commit. I attempted to record an early `caused_by` link to `d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231`, but the tracker refused it because it could not find a referencing commit for the target; I will still pass `--caused-by=d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231` on bug close.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is additive: plan-review `gate_status` includes whether this job’s REVIEW_RESULT findings are readable. `rg` found only MCP read registration, docs, and tests; no production caller relies on the absence of a findings-readability field. Existing status/verdict semantics remain unchanged.","timestamp":1788337912181097467},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress update: implemented and locally committed the gate_status/REVIEW_RESULT readiness fix at b5aad2979d72f6ad549d42af3b985e69007f3c08 in worktree /Users/joeoakhart/debug-gate-status-sidecar. Validation passed: targeted async gate tests, MCP schema coverage with the target tests, mutation tooth check, make lint, make typecheck, python -m rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models --check, and full make test with ambient Git config cleared (GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=0). Commit trailer verified with rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD. Gerrit push is currently blocked by external connectivity: repeated git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main attempts and HTTPS/SSH probes to rebar.solutions.navateam.com fail with SSL/banner timeouts. No design-decision escalation was hit; landing/closing remain pending until Gerrit is reachable.","timestamp":1788358192055117001}],"created_at":1788332684139080595,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7af0a8d0-e56e-4a6d-94db-5568f4bba6a2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa"},{"link_uuid":"8cd42dd2-6860-4b6a-8357-7502318963c3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c4cf-6dde-45b4-4dc6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`review_plan_start(ticket)` returns a `job_id`; callers poll `gate_status(job_id)` and then read retained `REVIEW_RESULT` findings. The bug is that a terminal plan-review poll (`status:\"passed\"`, `verdict:\"BLOCK\"`) did not prove that the readable `REVIEW_RESULT` belonged to that same run. A caller reading \"latest findings\" could silently consume a prior run's findings.\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 on ticket `549b-9cc5-940e-46c3`: job `1788326596882647223-94573cf0d90d404e87c74855306c16f2` reported terminal BLOCK while the newest readable sidecar was prior-run file `1788325963941841589-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json`; the current sidecar `1788327281362056852-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json` appeared later.\n\n## Root cause / actual layer\n\n`review_plan()` already calls `sidecar.emit()` before `_spawn_gate_daemon()` records the terminal `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` entry. The defect is not a simple in-process order inversion; it is missing per-run sidecar identity:\n\n- `sidecar.emit()` was best-effort and returned only a bool.\n- `_spawn_gate_daemon()` discarded sidecar outcome/identity when writing the terminal run index.\n- `gate_run_status()` reported terminal status plus attestation currency only. For BLOCK, the attestation is unsigned by definition, so `durable` cannot prove findings readiness.\n- `sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket)` is newest-by-ticket, not job-scoped.\n\nThus a terminal run without an exact sidecar receipt cannot distinguish current findings from stale latest findings, an unreadable tracker view, a legacy index, or permanent sidecar failure.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nAdd an exact receipt while preserving existing contracts.\n\n1. `_commands._seam.append_event()` returns the event-envelope timestamp as an additive receipt; existing callers may ignore it.\n2. `plan_review.sidecar.emit()` still returns bool, and also stamps `verdict[\"sidecar_reviewed_at\"]` with the timestamp returned by `append_event()`.\n3. `plan_review.__init__` keeps `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"]` boolean semantics unchanged while carrying that stamped receipt on the verdict.\n4. Reuse short-circuits that return current stored findings (`reuse.idempotent_reuse` and `reuse.verdict_reuse`) set `sidecar_reviewed_at` from the reused sidecar's filename timestamp while keeping `sidecar_emitted=false` because they did not write a new sidecar. Drift refresh/cancellation remain no-new-findings paths.\n5. `_mcp_llm._spawn_gate_daemon()` copies `sidecar_emitted` and any exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` from the completed review result into the terminal run index.\n6. `gate_status(job_id)` adds `findings` for plan-review jobs: `sidecar_type`, `readable`, `reason`, `reviewed_at`, `latest_reviewed_at`, and legacy diagnostic `job_started_at`.\n7. `findings.readable=true` only when a file with the exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` prefix exists and parses as a supported `plan_review_result_v1/v2` payload. It never infers freshness from newest timestamp or job start time.\n\nDisposition: no `findings` block is attached when the job is `unknown` because there is no indexed ticket/gate type. For indexed plan-review jobs, `findings.sidecar_type` is always `REVIEW_RESULT`. `current-review-result-sidecar` is readable. `sidecar-not-emitted` is a new record with `sidecar_emitted=false` and no receipt; `review-result-generation-unknown` is a legacy terminal record with no receipt fields; `run-failed` is a terminal gate failure with no review result; `run-stale-running` is a crashed-leader unavailable state. `review-result-sidecar-missing` covers absent, unreadable, corrupt, or unsupported exact-prefix files; callers may keep polling only under their normal bounded wait policy and must not read latest findings while false. `run-running` and `run-attaching` mean keep polling.\n\n## Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`: additive timestamp return from `append_event()`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`: stamp `sidecar_reviewed_at` while preserving bool return; reuse reads exact payload timestamps from existing `all_review_results()`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: verified call site; bool `sidecar_emitted` remains unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py`: carry reused current sidecar receipts on no-new-sidecar paths.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`: store the exact completed-review receipt in the terminal async run index.\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`: compute the plan-review `findings` readability block.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json`: document/model additive fields.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py` and `tests/interfaces/store/test_sidecar_reader.py`: regression and receipt tests.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`: document waiting for `findings.readable` before reading findings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Seed an old `REVIEW_RESULT`, record a terminal newer run with expected `sidecar_reviewed_at`, omit that sidecar, and assert `gate_status` is terminal with `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-sidecar-missing\"`.\n- [ ] Write the expected current sidecar and assert the same job reports `findings.readable=true` with `reason=\"current-review-result-sidecar\"`.\n- [ ] Drive two successive runs and assert poll-then-read returns no findings for the newer job until that job's exact sidecar is readable.\n- [ ] Assert terminal `sidecar_emitted=false` without a receipt reports `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`.\n- [ ] Assert terminal `sidecar_emitted=false` with a reused `sidecar_reviewed_at` reports `findings.readable=true` for that exact sidecar.\n- [ ] Assert exact-prefix corrupt or unsupported sidecar files report `findings.readable=false` with `reason=\"review-result-sidecar-missing\"`.\n- [ ] Assert `findings.latest_reviewed_at` reflects the newest-by-ticket sidecar timestamp for diagnostics only and is not used to infer readability.\n- [ ] Assert an unknown job has no `findings` block.\n- [ ] Assert `findings.sidecar_type` is `REVIEW_RESULT`.\n- [ ] Assert the daemon records the exact receipt returned by `review_plan()` even when a newer same-ticket sidecar is already readable.\n- [ ] Assert legacy terminal records without a receipt report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-generation-unknown\"`, with `job_started_at` diagnostic only.\n- [ ] Assert non-terminal plan-review runs report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"run-<status>\"`, and `reviewed_at=null`.\n- [ ] Assert terminal failed plan-review runs without a review result report `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"run-failed\"`.\n- [ ] Validate with targeted pytest, MCP schema coverage, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing verdict computation or whether a BLOCK is a completed (`passed`) gate run.\n- Making `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars required for the verdict; they remain best-effort observability.\n- Changing `plan_review_status` or signed-attestation currency.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"The durable run index gate_status replays; the terminal transition or the reported shape must account for sidecar readability."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"The gate_status MCP read surface that reports status and verdict to the polling caller."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py","reason":"Unit tests holding a stubbed sidecar writer open to make the window deterministic, asserting the status contract before and after the write lands."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c4cf-6dde-45b4-4dc6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c13933c3-1107-48c8-bf9a-442af79b16d9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["mcp","plan-review","gate-runs"],"ticket_id":"01c4-cca2-ec11-4530","ticket_type":"bug","title":"gate_status reports a terminal verdict before its REVIEW_RESULT sidecar is readable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c13933c3-1107-48c8-bf9a-442af79b16d9","6ee419c7-1546-409f-846b-c99c1a3d3cd8","badd10d7-da6e-434d-88e1-4fc45ac608d8","b9e0f400-89b4-4204-aae3-effa7545551f","8cd42dd2-6860-4b6a-8357-7502318963c3","4a0034a2-9bd0-4a72-bb4c-6d75b6442c25","0fe53288-22e4-4d08-b1bd-f166b4d9a118","459f9ae2-41e9-4ced-95f5-a26f3dac1120","0924e174-027a-49e8-addd-5a9844c0f682","b94ad2b0-7b90-42d2-ab03-38ee0d675d6b","96b46d13-ea61-4af7-b627-4c29bc32c017","c564e800-cdba-4917-90b8-f59e5961f4ec","26c70a81-8c00-4160-9138-7a0f8ae69e66","fbe351bd-1448-488e-aa89-a1a592eb86d6","50fa9311-427d-4851-a082-2129a32c4db9","0e0749cc-fa03-42ec-8766-d421e7e6daac"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788373002348222548,"uuid":"95d69850-536e-4791-8a6c-ce1c3ff86cda"}